 "headline": "On 100 labelled synthetic images, Drishyam at a 30% pixel cap found 0.50 of ground-truth boxes using 0.29 of the image's pixels, versus 0.32 for 20%-overlap 512-px tiling using 1.63: 1.58x its recall (95% CI 1.38-1.85, 1.26x with one-box-per-class boxes, 2.52x with as-specified mixed boxes) at 0.18x its pixels, which meets the 0.9x-at-0.3x hypothesis. It is 1.10x a single 1024-px downscale (95% CI 1.01-1.20, 0.45 at 0.05 of the pixels), 0.94x L1 tiling (0.53 at 0.40) and 0.94x L2 tiling (0.53 at 0.10, the best grid), and 2.12x L0 tiling when a match needs IoU >= 0.3 (no contains-the-centre clause); its own boxes placed at random would score 0.03 (0.01 with IoU only)."
